{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeMQQTaTHHD8VEPXBjrJ9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01X8GaiRgEwnbtdHcw4vUejQ","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/pods/pod-qos/","prompt":"Reproduce the page's prose VERBATIM — do not paraphrase, summarize, or reword. Copy exact sentences. I need, word for word:\n1. The opening — what Quality of Service classes are, that Kubernetes classifies the Pods you run and assigns each Pod to a specific QoS class, and that Kubernetes uses that classification to influence how different Pods are handled / eviction decisions.\n2. \"Guaranteed\" — the full criteria list (every Container in the Pod must have a memory limit and a memory request; they must be the same; every Container must have a CPU limit and a CPU request; they must be the same) and what it says about these Pods being the most stringent / not being killed until they exceed limits / not evicted.\n3. \"Burstable\" — the full criteria (the Pod does not meet the criteria for Guaranteed; at least one container in the Pod has a memory or CPU request or limit).\n4. \"BestEffort\" — the full criteria (the Pod does not meet the criteria for Guaranteed or Burstable; the containers must have no memory or CPU limits or requests).\n5. Anything about \"Memory QoS with cgroup v2\", \"Some behavior is independent of QoS class\", and how QoS class relates to eviction / oom_score_adj.\n6. The exact field name where the QoS class is reported (status.qosClass) if mentioned.\nPreserve headings. Exact original wording only."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1928,"cache_read_input_tokens":89685,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1928},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":nul